course: dictionary
lesson: 2094
title: Contest: a game or an argument
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A contest is a game, race or competition where people try to win, like «a spelling contest» at school. When you meet the word, look for clues such as win, prize, points or places. Those clues tell you a contest is a game.
explain: «Maddie and Jake once had a monkey-bars contest, both fell off into the bark chips, both laughed and decided being friends was better than winning.» The clues are monkey-bars, fell off and winning. So a contest is a game where people try to win, and here the two friends decided that friendship mattered more.
explain: Contest can also be a verb. To contest something is to argue that it is wrong or unfair. In «many artists said it was unfair», the artists were arguing against a result. When you see contest as a verb, ask yourself: is someone arguing about something?
fact: Contest (noun) means a game, race or competition where people try to win, such as «a pie-eating contest» at the fair.
fact: Contest (verb) means to argue that something is wrong or unfair.
fact: «A cooking contest between neighbours» is fine as long as everyone is in on the joke.
fact: Being a good loser means you can enjoy a contest even when you do not win, just like Maddie and Jake.
fact: Check your meaning: swap in «a game where people try to win» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: Maddie and Jake had a monkey-bars contest. What is a contest? | A sort of rope | *A game or competition where people try to win | A friendly chat about the weather | A kind of bark chip
exercise: «Many artists said the prize was unfair, so they chose to contest it.» What does contest mean here? | To cook a meal for friends | *To argue that it is wrong or unfair | To win a race | To laugh at a joke
exercise: At a spelling contest, what are people trying to do? | Forget their names | Sleep under the desk | *Win | Hide the words
test: «A cooking contest between neighbours is fine as long as everyone is in on the joke.» What does this suggest a contest can be? | *A friendly game that everyone enjoys | A serious war | A quiet walk in the park | A dangerous race
test: Which sentence uses contest as a verb? | *Some people want to contest the result because they think it was unfair | The pie-eating contest is at the fair | The spelling contest starts at two o'clock | Maddie and Jake had a monkey-bars contest
exam: Which best explains what a contest is? | A kind of prize you get for lying | A kind of animal | *A game or competition where people try to win | A place where people sleep
